WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.968
-Our first guest tonight
is an Academy Award-nominated

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:05.601
and Emmy-winning actor who you
know from shows like "Cheers"

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:09.100
and "True Detective" and films
such as "White Men Can't Jump,"

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.300
and "Zombieland,"
and "Triangle of Sadness."

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.634
He stars in "Champions," which
opens in theaters March 10th.

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:15.634
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.701
-My name is Marcus Marakovich

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.834
and I am going to be
your basketball coach

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.167
for the next three months.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.534
-Nope.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.567
-Wait. What?

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:27.300
-I said nope.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.033
[ Basketball dribbling ]

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.167
-Is this something
he normally does?

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.267
-Nope.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:39.701
-That's Darius.
He's our best player.

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:44.033
I'm Johnny. I'm your homie
with an extra chromie.

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:45.267
-Whoa.

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.567
-Please welcome back to
the show, our friend,

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.300
Woody Harrelson, everybody.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:59.734
♪♪

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:08.200
♪♪

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.767
Welcome back.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:12.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:16.534
-Listen, I know you guys
are here to see Niall,

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:17.767
but I appreciate that.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:20.033
-Very nice of them.
Very nice of them.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.300
How do you think I -
-I'm happy to see Niall, too.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.300
-Yeah.
-Like, I saw him backstage.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.734
I was, like, fawning like
a little school girl. Any way.

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.701
-That's very nice that
you can be honest about that.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.000
-Yeah.
-I felt the same way.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.601
I saw Niall backstage
and I had the same reaction.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:35.901
-But yeah, my - my daughter,
Mac, is, like, a huge fan.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:38.667
And so, you know,
she woke us up the other night

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.100
when he dropped his single.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.434
-Dude.
-It woke us up.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.200
Like - we're like -

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.767
-At what time can you wake up
Woody Harrelson?

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.300
Like, what - what's a good time?

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.801
-I don't think it's ever
a good idea.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.200
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.133
-Let a sleeping Woody lie?
-Exactly.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:56.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.901
-Now you - I should stress,
you needed a little sleep

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:01.501
because you did one of the great
late night endeavors.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:04.300
Last Saturday, you hosted "SNL"
for your fifth time.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.634
-Yeah.
-Fantastic episode.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.734
-Yeah, that was -
that was exciting.

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.801
-And I - let me say,
the five-Timers club --

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.300
the real accomplishment,
you didn't just knock out

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.868
five hosting stints
in seven years.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.267
You stretched this out.
-Yeah.

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:19.534
-It speaks to the breadth
of your career.

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:21.234
Your first one was 1989.

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:24.033
Do you remember your first time
hosting "SNL"?

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.634
-Not even a little bit.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:26.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.100
-Well, hold - let me reframe it.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.367
Do you remember much
about last Saturday?

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:31.901
-Nothing. Nothing at all.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:36.634
That's -- even then, I didn't --
I know that I left after --

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:39.033
-Yeah.
-After, at 6:00.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.033
-Yeah.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:43.634
-So, that's where my memory
started.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:44.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.000
-Yeah.
-Amazing.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.701
-But is it - do you remember -
the high of hosting?

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.434
Does that feel the same,
even though you're doing it

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:51.734
for your fifth time?

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:54.734
-Oh, there was a serious high
of hosting going on.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.133
-I walked -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:59.434
-I promise I'm not trying
to walk right into this.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:04.200
-Everyone in the dressing room
had a whole high of hosting.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.834
-So, you're saying
it's almost contagious

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:08.067
when they're around you.
-It was contagious.

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.300
-Yeah.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.467
Thick with -- anyway.

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:13.167
-Hey, this is very exciting.

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:16.534
So, you have your own --
your own weed dispensary?

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.367
-I do.
-Congratulations.

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:20.234
-Yeah, yeah.
-The Woods?

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:22.901
-The Woods.
-And this is an L.A. billboard,

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.601
and this is an old photo of you.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:28.300
-Yeah.
-Now, I was thinking, like,

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.501
what do you think this young man
would think if you told him

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:32.467
in the future,
you're going to own

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:35.400
a legal marijuana dispensary?

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.467
-Well, at the time,
he didn't smoke.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.534
-Really?

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:40.367
-So, he would have been like,
"No way."

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.834
I was very religious
at that time.

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:47.701
This is -- I was working as
a lifeguard at a --

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:52.334
anyway, someone sent this to --
it was at a church camp.

00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:53.701
I didn't want to get into
all that.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:56.601
But okay.
So, I used to go to church.

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:58.534
Anyway, yeah.

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:01.934
So, someone sent that to
The Woods.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.868
-Yeah.
-And then we were like,

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:06.167
"Well, let's just use this."
-Yeah.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.934
I will say, yeah -- I mean,
I would have definitely guessed

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:10.767
"weed" before
"church camp lifeguard."

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.100
Based on the photo.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.234
Well, that's very exciting.
Have you enjoyed it?

00:04:16.234 --> 00:04:18.901
I mean, it must be a nice moment
to be able to --

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.767
I mean, this is something you've
been a fan of for a while.

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:24.234
-Well, it's really
the most beautiful place

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.300
you've ever seen.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.000
I mean,
it is stunningly beautiful.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.100
Thomas Schoos, who is a partner,
did the designing,

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.834
and he's, like --
he's a brilliant designer.

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:37.167
So, it's, like --
it's beautiful.

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:39.467
It's the most beautiful
dispensary in the world.

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:41.300
After that,
I can't promise anything.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:45.133
But there is - there's
a ganja giggle garden out back

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:48.367
where you can go out there
and, um, giggle.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:49.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.400
-It's a giggle garden.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.868
This was amazing.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:56.200
Somebody -- in our lives, every
now and then, we might encounter

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:59.300
who we or other people will say
is your doppelganger.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.601
Right? You lay eyes on them
and you go, "Oh, my God,

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.701
I can't believe I lived my whole
life and there's a person

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:04.834
on earth who looks
just like me."

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:05.834
-I can't wait to see this.
-Well, this is --

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:08.467
somebody posted this on Twitter.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:09.567
You responded to it.

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:10.934
Their daughter --
their infant daughter.

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:12.934
-Oh, yes, yes.
-Yeah.

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.501
-And I was like, "How can an
infant daughter look like

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:16.767
Woody Harrelson?"
-Spitting image.

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.334
-I mean, that's insane.

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:21.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:27.734
-What a trip.
-Yeah.

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:30.634
I mean, can you imagine
how messed up

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:32.033
she's going to be in life?

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.200
Later, people are showing her
this picture.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.601
-I think she'll be --
I think she's gonna --

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:41.467
They say all babies grow out
of their Woody phase, yeah.

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:42.834
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:45.200
-I've got a lot more questions,
including about the film.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.634
We'll be right back with more
from Woody Harrelson.

